     "front": "Temporal vs spatial locality?",
     "back": "Temporal: reuse the same data soon. Spatial: use nearby data soon. Caches exploit both."
    },
    {
     "front": "Process vs thread?",
     "back": "Process: isolated address space. Thread: shared address space within a process — shared memory is the power and the peril."
    },
    {
     "front": "ACID?",
     "back": "Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability — the transaction contract."
    },
    {
     "front": "3NF in one line?",
     "back": "Every non-key attribute depends on the key, the whole key, and nothing but the key."
    },
    {
     "front": "Test pyramid order?",
     "back": "Many fast unit tests at the base, fewer integration, fewest slow e2e at the top."
    },
    {
     "front": "Scheduler starvation?",
     "back": "A waiting task never gets CPU. Classic cause: priorities without aging. The fix is aging — the longer a task waits, the higher its priority climbs. (Concepts note: scheduling.)"
    },
    {
     "front": "inode?",
     "back": "The filesystem's metadata record: permissions, ownership, block pointers — everything about a file except its name, which lives in the directory entry. (Concepts note.)"
