    "__init__ then __del__",
    "open() then close()",
    "try then catch"
   ],
   "answer": 0,
   "explain": "The context-manager protocol: __enter__ sets up, __exit__ cleans up — even when exceptions fly."
  },
  {
   "id": "il03-m16",
   "type": "choice",
   "q": "`len(x)` works when x defines ___.",
   "choices": [
    "__len__",
    "__iter__",
    "size()",
    "length"
   ],
   "answer": 0,
   "explain": "Dunder methods are the protocols — __len__ is the sized-duck protocol (duck typing, Module 1)."
  },
  {
   "id": "il03-m17",
   "type": "choice",
   "q": "From `List<? extends Number>` (producer) you can safely read elements as ___.",
